'''South Ayorin''' ({{Langx|yo|Àyórin Gúúsù}}), officially the '''Republic of Ayorin''' ({{Lang|bl|Orilẹ-ede Àyórin}}). The First Republic was founded on 10 March 1934 after the transfer of government responsibilities following the [[Partition of Burawa]] and becoming the first independent republican government in Ayori history. [[Chijindum Newke]] became the first [[President of Ayorin]] following a [[1934 Ayori general election|snap election]], and the [[National Assembly of South Ayorin|National Assembly]] in [[Ibadan]] promulgated Ayorin's first constitution in September, establishing a presidential system of government.

The republic rejected the Illypnian colonial presence in North Ayorin and claimed sovereignty over the entirety of Ayorin proper, but only held power south of the [[## Parallel]], more popularly known as the [[Line of Servitude]]. The First Republic was characterized by a swift [[Ayori Renaissance|cultural revolution]], moderate economic development, strong social and economic reform, and by the mid-1940s strong nationalist sentiment. Rapid negotiations in the early 1950s led to the Republic's invasion and liberation of [[North Ayorin]] in 194x.

